// Records the assignment of a filament preset to a slot on a printer with three slots. Slot 2 is assigned
// through each route: a pick in its selector in the sidebar (its list opened with click and the row clicked),
// the select_preset tool, and the plugin API's orca.host.preset.filament.begin_update(2, name) run from
// run_script; for an ordinary change to a filament with a default colour and to one without, and for a change to
// a support filament, under each value of the automatic flush calculation (Preferences > Behaviour > Auto flush
// after changing...). Then the plugin API's other forms, unsaved changes in the preset the filament tab edits,
// the refusals (no such slot, no such name, an incompatible preset, a mixed-colour slot) and a hidden preset. Each
// case starts from slot presets, colours and flushing volumes set to sentinels by fixtures/ops_presets.py, and
// after each call reads what it left once queued events have settled (the slot mapping, the edited filament
// preset, the three colour settings, the project's colours and flushing volumes, dialogs, undo snapshots).
// Refused calls are optional. Run it on a freshly launched app (a hidden preset stays shown until a restart)
// with
//   tools/mcp/orca_mcp.py run-replay tools/mcp/tests/ops_assign_filament_preset_multi_slot.json --out <dir>
{
  "orca_replay": 1,
  "name": "ops assign_filament_preset, several slots",
  "steps": [
    {"tool": "wait", "args": {"for": "ready"}},
    {"tool": "new_project", "args": {"discard_changes": true, "preset_changes": "discard"}},
